Read the size of a manifest file with FileStandardInformation.

get_manifest_in_manifest_file asked NtQueryInformationFile for
FileEndOfFileInformation, a class Wine's server answers but Windows only
accepts in NtSetInformationFile: on the layer's NT (the host's) the query fails
with STATUS_INVALID_INFO_CLASS, so no .manifest file ever parsed. A dependency
found in winsxs\manifests or a private assembly next to the program
(Chrome's <version>\<version>.manifest, which lists chrome_elf.dll) then failed,
and with it the whole activation context of the program
(docs/slices/laptop-programs.md). FileStandardInformation carries the same
EndOfFile on both.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c b/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
index 47464d4..9c14cfc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
@@ -3055,7 +3055,7 @@ static NTSTATUS get_manifest_in_pe_file( struct actctx_loader* acl, struct assem
 static NTSTATUS get_manifest_in_manifest_file( struct actctx_loader* acl, struct assembly_identity* ai,
                                                LPCWSTR filename, LPCWSTR directory, BOOL shared, HANDLE file )
 {
-    FILE_END_OF_FILE_INFORMATION info;
+    FILE_STANDARD_INFORMATION info;
     IO_STATUS_BLOCK io;
     HANDLE              mapping;
     OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES   attr;
@@ -3081,7 +3081,7 @@ static NTSTATUS get_manifest_in_manifest_file( struct actctx_loader* acl, struct
     NtClose( mapping );
     if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS) return status;
 
-    status = NtQueryInformationFile( file, &io, &info, sizeof(info), FileEndOfFileInformation );
+    status = NtQueryInformationFile( file, &io, &info, sizeof(info), FileStandardInformation );
     if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
         status = parse_manifest(acl, ai, filename, NULL, directory, shared, base, info.EndOfFile.QuadPart);
 
